# Have food: leave a shelter if the body is sealed in, then hunt. A core skill
# so the brain can set "have food" as a goal (the arbiter's hunger need wakes
# the brain when no food is held, see arbiter.rs): hunting runs for minutes, so
# it is a goal with a budget, not a need that takes the body at the survival
# tier. At night the brain sets it only when the food bar is critical
# (decision 2026-11-10 "Hungry at night: hunt only when it is critical").
#
# Why the rules are ordered this way: the goal check is on top, so a body that
# already holds n food items stays where it is, sealed in or not. Next, a body
# sealed in (`sheltered()`) opens the shelter and climbs out first
# (`leave_shelter`): no animal is in sight from inside, and a hunt that starts
# there fails and leaves the body shut in (run 9, third review). A shelter that
# cannot be left (`no_exit`, `unsafe`) is retried and fails the skill after the
# third failure; the caller decides what then. An open body, or one whose
# `sheltered()` perception cannot answer (an unknown guard never fires), hunts
# with `hunt_food`, which holds the hunting rules: the six-rule limit leaves
# no room for them here.
skill get_food(n: int = 2)
  doc "Have n food items: leave a shelter if sealed in, then hunt animals for meat."
  rules:
    count_food() >= $n -> done
    sheltered() -> leave_shelter()
    true -> do hunt_food($n)
